@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# draft-advisor-master-data: Read advisor master data from the ERP
+
+- **Jira:** none yet
+- **Gate:** design (trigger 2)
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:** <GitHub login> <YYYY-MM-DD>
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: integration (public API `readAdvisor`), erp-port (new operation), erp-fake (seed data), apps/worker (wiring)
+
+## Context
+
+Head office needs the advisor master data from the ERP (T2-C-010). The identity module exposes it; the ERP is reached only through `integration` (T3-D-005). Decision: [ADR-0017](../../adr/0017-erp-advisor-master-data-read.md).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+The register has no AC for this need. Covered capability and decisions:
+
+| ID | Test |
+|---|---|
+| T2-C-010 | `packages/core/src/identity/identity.test.ts`, `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts`, `packages/erp-fake/src/erp-fake.test.ts` |
+| T2-D-009 | `packages/core/src/integration/integration.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** identity: `createIdentity({ repo, bus, integration, clock })`; `.getAdvisor(advisorNumber): Promise<Advisor | null>`; type `Advisor` = `{ advisorNumber, givenName, familyName, email, active, sourceVersion, readAt }`; invariant: reads on each call, stores nothing. integration: `readAdvisor(advisorNumber): Promise<ErpRead<AdvisorMasterData> | null>`. erp-port: `AdvisorMasterData`. erp-fake: `fakeAdvisors`.
+- **Contracts:** ERP port operation `readAdvisor(advisorNumber)` → `AdvisorMasterData | null`. Payload: `advisorNumber` (`^B\d{5}$`), `givenName`, `familyName`, `email`, `active` (boolean), `sourceVersion`. Throws `ErpUnavailableError` when the ERP is down.
+- **Schema:** none. The data is not stored.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- `getAdvisor` returns a flat record, not an `ErpRead`: the caller asked for this shape. `sourceVersion` and `readAt` keep the T2-D-009 fields; `source` is always `erp` and is left out.
+- `integration` becomes a required dependency of `createIdentity`: `getAdvisor` cannot work without it.
+- A malformed advisor number is passed to the ERP, which returns `null`. No separate validation error.
+- Fake advisor `B20001` (Clara Beispiel, active, `sourceVersion` `v2`) is the advisor of the fake customer `K100001`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- A stored copy of advisor data, its refresh and reconciliation.
+- The advisor structure and customer assignments.
+- A head office portal screen.
+
+## Open questions
+
+None.
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
